# AbarVa — Cursor Rules

## Visual reference (binding)

The canonical visual reference for Strategic Moves and all derived
surfaces (Maestro P1–P7, Detail, Originate, future Charter/Decision/
Run) lives at `docs/design/strategic-moves/`:

- `tokens.css` — single source of truth for colors, type, spacing,
  radius, motion. Never introduce new tokens. Never adjust values.
- `14-strategic-moves-home.html` — high-fidelity prototype of all
  three views (#dashboard-view, #detail-view, #originate-view).
  Pixel-match the layout when implementing.
- `README.md` — implementation brief (acceptance checklist at end).
- `INTEGRATION.md` — what to touch, what to leave alone, token
  substitutions (especially the --gold → --abarva-signal-blue rule).

## Token discipline (hard rule)

- Use only tokens defined in `tokens.css` (brand or canon section).
- The `--gold` value used in the prototype is NOT canonical. Replace
  with `--abarva-signal-blue` per INTEGRATION.md mapping table.
- No new colors, no new fonts, no new radius values, no gradients,
  no decorative SVG icons, no emoji, no stock illustration.

## Type ramp (hard rule)

- Display headings: Fraunces 500/700 (--abarva-serif).
- UI body: Inter 400/500/600 (--abarva-sans).
- Mono eyebrows / labels / code: JetBrains Mono 600 (--abarva-mono),
  uppercase, letter-spacing 0.12em.
- Mono eyebrows are the most distinctive AbarVa typographic gesture.
  Never replace with sans-serif uppercase.

## Surface vocabulary (hard rule)

Two surfaces, one brand:

- Public/marketing/investor: paper background (#faf7f1), navy ink
  (#0c1a3a), signal blue accent (#0066CC).
- Authenticated app (this is where Strategic Moves lives): cream
  background (--canon-bg-cream #f5f1eb), white surface cards, ink
  text. Status colors (red/amber/teal) are semantic only, never
  decorative.

## Naming doctrine (hard rule)

- External UI vocabulary: "Strategic Move" / "Move" / "your moves"
- Internal substrate: `engagements` table, `program_*` mid-layer.
  Database table renames are forbidden.
- Browser URL routes user-facing: `/strategic-moves`,
  `/strategic-moves/[moveId]`, `/strategic-moves/new`.
- API routes stay at `/api/v1/programs/*`. Response field names like
  `programId` stay. Code identifiers like `getProgramById` stay.
- Rule: if a string is read by a user, rebrand. If read by a
  developer, keep.

## Phase model (hard rule)

Strategic Moves runs a six-phase model — P0..P5. AbarVa does not
execute the transformation. After P5 Mobilize & Handoff, Control
Tower owns execution tracking, value realization, and risk monitoring.
Build / Execute / Verify are NOT Strategic Move phases.

Binding reference: `docs/design/strategic-moves/PHASE_MODEL_V2_DOCTRINE.md`.

Use the static lookup `src/lib/programs/phase-labels.ts` for all
user-visible phase references:

  0 → "P0 Originate"               (short: "Originate")
  1 → "P1 Charter"                 (short: "Charter")
  2 → "P2 Discover & Diagnose"     (short: "Diagnose")
  3 → "P3 Design Future State"     (short: "Design")
  4 → "P4 Roadmap & Business Case" (short: "Roadmap")
  5 → "P5 Mobilize & Handoff"      (short: "Mobilize")

Never hard-code phase labels inline. Never reintroduce P6/P7 as
Strategic Move phases. The rail surfaces a "→ Tower" terminal
indicator after P5 — that is a different surface, not a phase.

## Component reuse (hard rule)

The Phase Rail (`<PhaseRail current={n} />`) is shared across Detail,
Originate, and all future phase surfaces. Build once at
`src/components/strategic-moves/PhaseRail.tsx`, reuse everywhere. Do
not inline. The rail defaults to `totalPhases=6` from
`TOTAL_PHASES` in `phase-labels.ts`; do not pass `totalPhases={8}`.

## Hard "do not" list

- Do not ship the tweaks panel from the prototype to production.
- Do not introduce the `--gold` token to `tokens.css`.
- Do not use the signal-blue CTA color for in-app primary actions
  (use ink-on-cream black). Signal blue is reserved for public
  surfaces and one-per-page accents.
- Do not gate edit rights on "participant on move" status. Any
  tenant_member can edit any move (locked access decision).
- Do not bypass app-layer tenant filters on Strategic Moves
  routes — the simplified access model treats client_id scoping
  as a hard wall.

## PR creation workflow

If `gh` CLI is not authenticated in the agent shell, do not run
`gh pr create` or `gh pr merge` — they will fail. Instead:

1. Push the branch via `git push origin <branch-name>`
2. Output to the user:
   - The exact branch name
   - A suggested PR title (one line)
   - A suggested PR description (markdown, ready to paste)
3. Stop. The user creates and merges the PR via the GitHub UI.

If `gh` CLI is authenticated (cloud agent with GH_TOKEN), `gh pr create`
is fine. Either path is acceptable — just don't get stuck retrying.
